# UI Component Standards

All interactive components **must** be built on [ShadCN](https://ui.shadcn.com/) primitives (Radix UI + CVA) to inherit correct ARIA roles, keyboard navigation, and focus management for free.

## Rules

- **Never** use a plain HTML interactive element when a ShadCN equivalent exists:
  - `<select>` → `Select` from `@radix-ui/react-select`
  - `<dialog>` → `Dialog` from `@radix-ui/react-dialog`
  - `<button>` → use the shared `Button` component (`packages/ui/src/components/button.tsx`) unless very simple inline usage where the raw `<button>` is fine
  - Checkboxes, radios, switches, tooltips, popovers, etc. → Radix primitives

- All ShadCN component files live in `packages/ui/src/components/` and follow the standard ShadCN file shape:
  - Named exports only (no default export)
  - Typed with `React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef` or `React.HTMLAttributes`
  - Composed via `cn()` from `packages/ui/src/lib/utils.ts`
  - CVA (`class-variance-authority`) for variant APIs

- When adding a new Radix package, add it to `packages/ui/package.json` (not to individual apps).

- Export new primitives from `packages/ui/src/index.ts`.

## Where ShadCN components live

```
packages/ui/src/components/
  badge.tsx         ← Badge (CVA)
  button.tsx        ← Button (CVA + Radix Slot)
  card.tsx          ← Card family
  carousel.tsx      ← Embla carousel
  dialog.tsx        ← Radix Dialog
  input.tsx         ← Input (CVA)
  select.tsx        ← Radix Select  ← add if missing
  separator.tsx     ← Radix Separator
  ...
```
